electron/node_modules/
*.db
*.db-journal
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build/test artifacts. electron/tsconfig.node.json sets composite: true,
# which makes tsc emit .tsbuildinfo; vite/vitest write a timestamped temp
# config bundle on every run (observed directly: this fails to write under
# a read-only sandbox, which is how the gap was found).
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
*.timestamp-*.mjs
vite.config.*.timestamp-*
vitest.config.*.timestamp-*

# Gold-fixture eval run artifacts and the judge-response cache — benchmark
# logs, not reviewed artifacts (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-09-gold-eval-harness-design.md §9).
# Promoting a specific run to a checked-in snapshot is a deliberate, manual
# action, not something this ignore rule should auto-exempt.
.eval-runs/

# macOS
.DS_Store

